// EXPECT: E0254 — `context` in a `#c_call` procedure (ADR-0057 §3)
//
// A `#c_call` procedure receives no implicit context — that is the whole meaning of the opt-out
// (ADR-0001) — so `context` inside one has nothing to denote. Distinct from E0201 "unresolved name"
// deliberately: `context` is a keyword and always "resolves", so reporting it as an unknown name
// would send the reader looking for a declaration to add rather than telling them this procedure has
// no context by design.
//
// Two shapes here: a `#c_call` procedure, and a `#foreign`-adjacent one — sema makes every `#foreign`
// procedure implicitly `#c_call`, so a `context` in a body it *could* have (a `#foreign` declaration
// has none) is covered by the same rule; that half is unobservable without a body, so only the
// explicit `#c_call` is exercised.
raw :: () -> s64 #c_call {
    return context.allocator;
}
